et\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}(2x^{3} + kx^{2})dx &= [\\frac{x^{4}}{2} + \\frac{kx^{3}}{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{k}{3}] - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{k}{3} + \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac k3+\\dfrac{1}{2} = 1 \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad k=\\dfrac{3}{2}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186105246 17592186105247 17592186105248 17592186105249 17592186105250 17592186105348 17592186105349 17592186105350 17592186105351 17592186105352] "immutable_fields" [[17592186105245 :answer-field/correct] [17592186105245 :answer-field/id] [17592186105245 :answer-field/key] [17592186105245 :answer-field/type] [17592186105347 :answer-field/correct] [17592186105347 :answer-field/id] [17592186105347 :answer-field/key] [17592186105347 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
